#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:11
msgid "Before starting to log a QSO, please note the basic rules."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:13
msgid "- Each new QSO should be on a new line."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:14
msgid ""
"- On each new line, only write data that has changed from the previous QSO."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:17
msgid "The first QSO"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:18
#, php-format
msgid ""
"To begin, ensure you have already filled in the form on the left with the "
"date, station call, and operator's call. The main data includes the band (or "
"QRG in MHz, e.g., %s), mode, and time. After the time, you provide the first "
"QSO, which is essentially the callsign."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:23
msgid "For example, a QSO that started at 21:34 (UTC) with 4W7EST on 20m SSB."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:25
msgid "Signal reports (RST)"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:26
msgid ""
"If you don't provide any RST information, the syntax will use 59 for phone, "
"599 for CW and +0 dB for digital data modes. Our next QSO wasn't 59 on both "
"sides, so we provide the information with the sent RST first. It was 2 "
"minutes later than the first QSO."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:32
msgid ""
"The first QSO was at 21:34, and the second one 2 minutes later at 21:36. We "
"write down 6 because this is the only data that changed here. The "
"information about band and mode didn't change, so this data is omitted."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:34
msgid "Date and time"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:35
msgid ""
"For our next QSO at 21:40 on 14th May, 2021, we changed the band to 40m but "
"still on SSB. If no RST information is given, the syntax will use 59 for "
"every new QSO. Therefore we can add another QSO which took place at the "
"exact same time two days later. The date must be in format YYYY-MM-DD."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:47
msgid "Additional information"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:48
msgid "Additional informations can be submitted in the following way:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:49
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:53
msgid "Operator Name:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:57
msgid "QSL-message (Caution! Not visible in wavelog currently!):"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:61
msgid ""
"You may use the comment syntax, to fill adif-fields supported by the Wavelog-"
"Import:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:66
msgid "Contest exchange"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:67
msgid "Contest exchange; serials or other exchange - or even both:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:74
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Received exchange has to be prefixed with a dot %s, sent exchange with a "
"comma %s. The last two lines are equivalent - i.e. spaces don't matter as "
"the order doesn't as well. Each of the four lines above simply illustrates "
"one type of exchange (serial only, text only, or both); note that the sent "
"exchange is 'sticky': once set, it is automatically carried into the "
"following QSOs (whenever the next line contains a received exchange or a "
"single comma %s) until you change or wipe it. To automatically increment the "
"sent serial, add %s to a QSO line together with an initial sent exchange (it "
"does not work on its own line). To deactivate, use %s:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:79
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Here, the first qso uses the set serial 1, and the second will use 2 as the "
"serial. If you want to wipe your sent exchange, use %s:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:84
#, php-format
msgid ""
"First, all previous exchange is wiped, then only a serial is set. Otherwise "
"the previous exchange %s would have been set also."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:86
msgid "Time zone"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:87
#, php-format
msgid ""
"If you log in local time instead of UTC, declare your offset once with %s "
"(or the short form %s) followed by the signed hour offset. All following QSO "
"times are then converted to UTC until you change the offset again:"
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:92
msgid "Here, the QSO logged at 14:00 local time is stored as 12:00 UTC."
msgstr ""

#: application/views/simplefle/syntax_help.php:95
#, php-format
msgid ""
"A full summary of all commands and the necessary syntax can be found in "
"%sthis article%s of our Wiki."
msgstr ""

